---
import { site } from "../config";
---

<!-- Why the practice is called what it is. The motto lives here, explained,
     rather than as a slogan in the hero. -->
<section id="name" class="bg-green-deep py-20 text-paper lg:py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 lg:px-8">
    <p class="label text-paper/65">On the name</p>
    <p
      class="mt-6 max-w-4xl font-display text-[clamp(2rem,4.6vw,3.6rem)] italic leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.015em]"
    >
      {site.name}, {site.tagline.charAt(0).toLowerCase() + site.tagline.slice(1)}
    </p>
    <div class="mt-10 grid max-w-4xl gap-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-paper/80 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-12">
      <p>
        In Latin, <em class="font-display not-italic text-paper">robur</em> means
        oak, the hard timber, and also strength.
        It's where the English word <em>robust</em> comes from.{" "}
        <em class="font-display not-italic text-paper">Ignis</em> is fire.
      </p>
      <p>
        AI is making things feel unstable right now, and the name has two
        meanings for me. It's the strength to withstand the fire, and also the
        strength of the fire. Together they stand for a balanced approach, one part realism and
        one part optimism.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
